<task id="040" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Email: compose widget, spaarke_compose_email (model-visible), app-only spaarke_send_email</title>
    <phase>3 Email, evaluation and E2E</phase>
    <gate>r1 gate RELEASED 2026-11-25 (joint mcp-r1/mcp-r2 determination under the owner's delegation; see notes/decisions.md D-r1-gate). Before starting, merge origin/master into this branch (merge, never rebase). Do not edit r1's ISS-010 files (DecisionCommitService, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, RecordCreationService, CallerWriteAuthorization, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerMetadataReadMemo, AssignTaskNotifier, the email-bell job handler) or the Decision wizard heading files (DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx, Worklist/IssueLine.tsx, composeIssueLine.ts) without messaging mcp-r1 first.</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>The project's only irreversible write (email send) behind CommunicationService's filters; new widget; tags include security and auth</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Irreversible send path: app-only visibility, idempotency against double send, reuse of CommunicationAuthorizationFilter / CommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter checks without copying; project brief raises 040</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>K</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Last of the serialised widget tasks (shares McpModule.cs, Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj and publish-bff-artifact.yml with 034/035); also edits the communication filters</parallel-reason>
    <deps>011, 021, 023, 035, 039</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, security, auth, react, typescript, frontend, fluent-ui, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>10-12 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add email to Copilot within the owner's v1 scope: spaarke_compose_email (model-visible, no side effect) opens a compose widget pre-filled with a draft (To/Cc, subject, rich body, regarding matter, suggested documents); the widget src/client/widgets/spaarke-email-compose/ renders EmailComposer with task 011's MCP host over task 021's transport; spaarke_send_email is app-only, takes an idempotency key, applies the POST /api/communications/send authorization through a shared method (not a copy), sends through CommunicationService.SendAsync as the caller and archives to the matter with the attachments.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in the Spaarke communication core (ADR-045), MCP Apps visibility and Fluent v9.</role>
  <goal>The model can draft but never send; the user's Send in the widget sends once (retry with the same key does not double-send), archived to the regarding matter with the chosen matter documents; disabled senders and refused recipients return the service's reasonCode and send nothing; REST /api/communications/send bytes are unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-12, FR-16, NFR-01 (send p95 ≤ 15 s), NFR-06 (send app-only + idempotency key). REST: Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs POST /api/communications/send (:111) with CommunicationAuthorizationFilter and AddCommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter(CommunicationRecordRoute.Send) — caller must read every attached document and hold AppendTo on every association; filters in Api/Filters/Communication*.cs. Service: Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs SendAsync (:2412; request model Services/Communication/Models/SendCommunicationRequest.cs: To, Cc, Subject, Body, BodyFormat, Associations, SendMode, ArchiveToSpe, AttachmentDocumentIds, CorrelationId). No idempotency key exists on the send path today. Task 011: createMcpEmailComposeHandlers / useMcpEmailHostProps / McpToolCaller. Task 023: spaarke_list_documents for the attachment picker. Widget scaffold: tasks 034/035.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/CommunicationAuthorizationFilter.cs and CommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter.cs (Send checks exposed as one shared method; filters call it)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Email/ComposeEmailTool.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Email/SendEmailTool.cs (visibility ["app"])</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Email/EmailComposeWidgetResource.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/McpModule.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj</file>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/publish-bff-artifact.yml</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Mcp.Email.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Communication/CommunicationSendContractBaselineTests.cs (frozen REST bytes, recorded before the extraction)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/Email/SendEmailToolAuthTests.cs (app-only visibility; each REST refusal mirrored)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Mcp/Email/SendEmailToolTests.cs (one send per key; archive to matter with attachments)</file>
