  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">r1 gate RELEASED 2026-11-25 (joint mcp-r1/mcp-r2 determination under the owner's delegation; see notes/decisions.md D-r1-gate). Before starting, merge origin/master into this branch (merge, never rebase). Do not edit r1's ISS-010 files (DecisionCommitService, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, RecordCreationService, CallerWriteAuthorization, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerMetadataReadMemo, AssignTaskNotifier, the email-bell job handler) or the Decision wizard heading files (DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx, Worklist/IssueLine.tsx, composeIssueLine.ts) without messaging mcp-r1 first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Run as the caller (IHttpContextAccessor; UserContextRequired; no app-only identity fallback; never pass or log the token). The Send checks of both communication filters move into one shared method the filters and SendEmailTool call; the tool adds none; refusals map with the REST reasonCode (for example sdap.communication.*). The frozen-bytes baseline for POST /api/communications/send is written and green before the extraction and passes after.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">spaarke_send_email: visibility ["app"] only (never listed to the model), readOnlyHint false, destructiveHint true, idempotentHint true; required idempotencyKey; a retry with the same key and caller returns the first result and calls SendAsync once (key handling per r1's CompleteDecisionTool; a new store needs escalation). Regarding matter is required; AttachmentDocumentIds must belong to that matter (checked through the shared method's document-read check plus a same-matter check against spaarke_list_documents' source); archive to the matter (ArchiveToSpe/associations as the Console send does).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Idempotency key semantics (task 011 D4 and its verifier passes): store only successful or outcome-unknown attempts under the key; a definite 4xx refusal does not consume it. Bind the key to the payload: a reused key with a different payload (the user edited after an outcome-unknown failure) is refused with a clear reasonCode, never answered by replaying the first result. Reserve the key atomically so two overlapping sends with one key deliver once. Return status as an integer 400-599 in structuredContent (the client host does not clamp it). The widget must display the picker error outcome ({error, reference}) from task 011 and give the transport (task 021) a callTool timeout.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">spaarke_compose_email: model-visible, readOnlyHint true, no write; returns the draft in structuredContent and _meta.ui.resourceUri ui://spaarke/email-compose.html. No model-visible tool can send (asserted). Nothing relies on a host consent prompt (NFR-06).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Widget: EmailComposer through 011's useMcpEmailHostProps over 021's transport; v1 controls only (To/Cc, subject, rich body, regarding matter pre-set, attachments from the matter); _meta.ui.csp empty; no fetch/MSAL/Xrm; Fluent v9 semantic tokens; host light/dark; keyboard operable; bundle &lt; 1 MB target, 3 MB hard. Mcp:Enabled=false removes both tools and the resource (ADR-032).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Model-visible: draft fields the model supplied plus document names; never the sent body back, never other mailbox content. Logs: tool name, latency, recipient count, outcome/reasonCode, correlation id; never addresses, subject or body (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Send goes through CommunicationService.SendAsync only (the communication core); no direct Graph call.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source: spec.md 'Placement &amp; New Components'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, 55 MB total triggers architecture review, 60 MB is a hard stop. No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**, or the widget's own jest suite), mocks only at module boundaries (Graph sender), and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Node install: npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund (not npm ci). Before each push run bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master.</constraint>
  </constraints>

