  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Confirm the r1 gate and 011, 021, 023, 035, 039; read the send handler, both filters and SendAsync; record how the Console send sets Associations/ArchiveToSpe.</step>
    <step order="2">Write CommunicationSendContractBaselineTests and confirm it passes unchanged.</step>
    <step order="3">Expose the Send checks as one shared method; filters call it; the baseline still passes.</step>
    <step order="4">Write SendEmailTool (app-only, idempotent) and ComposeEmailTool; ledger rows; auth and data-mutation tests.</step>
    <step order="5">Write EmailComposeWidgetResource, register it, add the embed and CI steps; scaffold spaarke-email-compose with 011's host; widget tests; check-bundle-size.mjs.</step>
    <step order="6">Run communication, EmailComposer, MCP suites, ArchTests and conformance; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="8">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Send checks cannot be shared without changing REST bytes, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>If double-send protection needs a new store, STOP and escalate with the §11 answers (spec requires the key; storage is the open choice).</trigger>
    <trigger>If the host does not honour visibility ["app"] (the model can call send), STOP: do not ship the send tool; escalate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>CommunicationService.SendAsync and POST /api/communications/send with CommunicationAuthorizationFilter + CommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter (CAPABILITY-INDEX communication core, ADR-045); EmailComposer + 011's MCP host; 021's transport; r1's app-only idempotent CompleteDecisionTool; notes/reuse-scan.md rows "Email compose component" and "Email send".</existing>
    <extension>The service, filters (extended in place with a shared method), component and transport are reused; the two tools, one resource and one widget folder are the minimal new surface (one widget per component, owner Q5; send must be app-only, NFR-06).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Copilot users cannot compose or send matter email from Spaarke (FR-12 fails), and without the shared method the tool would copy filter checks, which the spec forbids.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Compose and send in Copilot Chat">
      <steps>
        <step>After deploy 049, ask "Draft an email to the client on matter {test matter} about the hearing date" with the Spaarke MCP source</step>
        <step>Verify the compose widget opens pre-filled (To, subject, body, regarding matter) and the attachment picker lists only that matter's documents</step>
        <step>Press Send with the keyboard; verify one email is sent and archived to the matter with the chosen attachment</step>
        <step>Ask the model to "send it now" without the widget; verify it cannot</step>
        <step>Check the widget console for errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Model drafts only; the user's Send sends once and archives; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the host to dark theme</step>
        <step>Verify the composer follows the host theme</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Fluent v9 semantic tokens only</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build; dotnet test</tool>
    <tool name="npm">build, jest and check-bundle-size in src/client/widgets/spaarke-email-compose</tool>
  </tools>

