  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">CommunicationSendContractBaselineTests pass before and after the extraction.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">tools/list as seen by the model contains spaarke_compose_email and not spaarke_send_email; spaarke_send_email carries visibility ["app"].</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A send with a new key calls SendAsync once with the regarding-matter association, archive on, and the chosen document ids; a retry with the same key calls it zero more times and returns the first result.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a disabled sender, a refused recipient, a document the caller cannot read and a document from another matter each return isError with the service/filter reasonCode and send nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a send without a regarding matter is refused before SendAsync.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Widget jest: v1 controls only; Send calls spaarke_send_email through the transport; zero fetch/Xrm calls. check-bundle-size.mjs ≤ 3 MB (recorded).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Logs captured in tests contain no address, subject or body text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ArchTests and conformance pass; publish-size delta recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-12, FR-16, NFR-01, NFR-05, NFR-06. Two adversarial-verifier passes (security, auth). uac-r2 reviews the filter extraction.</notes>

